locklyctl-mqtt - a self-hosted MQTT server and management backend for Lockly
Wi-Fi locks.

Not affiliated with, authorised by, or endorsed by Lockly Security Inc. /
PIN GENIE LIMITED. "Lockly" and the lock model names are trademarks of their
owner, used here only to identify the hardware.

The BLE frame crypto and builders in internal/lockly (AES key derivation,
master-code encoding, CRC-8, frame assembly, the 0x1E status, 0x33 time zone,
0x73 access-user and the 01 01 / 01 04 setup frames) are ported from locklyctl
(https://github.com/DigitalCyberSoft/locklyctl), which in turn ports them from
LocklyHA (https://github.com/Forcky/LocklyHA), Copyright (c) 2024 Patrick Forck,
under the MIT License. They are pinned to locklyctl by the test vectors.

Whether a given lock will connect to a non-Lockly broker (in particular over
TLS) is unverified hardware behaviour. See CONTRACT.md.
